@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# router_ceiling.dem — Story 5.6: the tier port ceilings, visual + pinned.
+# A mid router (8 ports) and a high router (16 ports) are placed and wired to
+# the fixture host: 8 parallel wide pipes mid(3)<->host(2) fill the mid's 8
+# ports, and 16 parallel standard pipes high(4)<->host(2) fill the high's 16.
+# The T2 captures show the FULL-ceiling state — a 9th pipe onto the mid / 17th
+# onto the high would reject .Router_Ports_Full (the reject count is pinned by
+# the core unit test test_mid_high_port_ceilings; a rejected command cannot
+# ride a demo's action log — it would latch replay_error and fail the gate,
+# so the golden is the ceiling state itself, the reject is the next draw).
+#
+# Geometry: mid at {20,5} (10 tiles from fixture router >= 4; 15.6 from host
+# <= wide max 18); high at {28,15} (8 from fixture router; 4 from host <= std
+# max 14; 12.8 from mid >= 4). Parallel pipes bundle (2.1) — each occupies one
+# port on the junction end (canon #14), the terminal end is unlimited.
+#
+# T2 captures: 2500ms pins both full pucks (mid 8 LEDs + glowing core; high
+# 16 LEDs + double light ring); 3500ms pins the settled topology. T1 + the
+# replay gate pin the fills byte-identically (E10).
+seed 42
+run 4000ms
+at 400ms place router_mid 20 5
+at 500ms place router_high 28 15
+at 600ms draw 3 2 wide
+at 600ms draw 3 2 wide
+at 600ms draw 3 2 wide
+at 600ms draw 3 2 wide
+at 600ms draw 3 2 wide
+at 600ms draw 3 2 wide
+at 600ms draw 3 2 wide
+at 600ms draw 3 2 wide
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+at 700ms draw 4 2 standard
+capture at 2500ms
+capture at 3500ms
+expect hash stable
