@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# router_tiers.dem — Story 5.6: the mid + high router tiers are placeable
+# hardware (GDD M3: basic 4 / mid 8 / high 16 ports, canon #14 + user ruling
+# 2026-08-14). The 1.2 fixture is residential(0) at {8,15} <- router(1) at
+# {20,15} -> content_host(2) at {32,15}. The player places router_mid(3) at
+# {20,5} (10 tiles from the fixture router >= the 4-tile router↔router rule)
+# and router_high(4) at {28,15} (8 tiles from the fixture router, 4 from the
+# host — the router↔terminal floor is 2). Both are LOGGED Cmd_Place_Router
+# entries (the same command kind + type_idx as basic — no new command, no
+# LOG_VERSION bump). Then a chain fixture-router → mid → high → host wires
+# the new tiers into the net (each draw spans <= standard max 14).
+#
+# T2 captures: 2500ms pins the settled placement + wiring with the tier-scaled
+# pucks (look-book A3: mid = +glowing core + 8 LEDs; high = double light
+# ring + 16 LEDs); 3500ms pins the settled topology. T1 hashes + the replay
+# gate pin placement + draw byte-identically (E10).
+seed 42
+run 4000ms
+at 400ms place router_mid 20 5
+at 500ms place router_high 28 15
+at 600ms draw 1 3 standard
+at 700ms draw 3 4 standard
+at 800ms draw 4 2 standard
+capture at 2500ms
+capture at 3500ms
+expect hash stable
